cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: ExforFissionData.jl
abstract: >-
  Retrieval of experimental fission observables from the IAEA EXFOR archive as tabulated data
  files, with a record of every dataset the query considered and why each was kept or excluded.
  Selection is driven by the EXFOR reaction code, and no normalisation is applied to retrieved
  ordinates.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gogîță
    given-names: Paul-Adrian
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulGoG/ExforFissionData.jl
keywords:
  - nuclear fission
  - nuclear data
  - EXFOR
  - fission fragment yields
  - prompt neutron multiplicity
  - Julia
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Towards a More Complete and Accurate Experimental Nuclear Reaction Data Library (EXFOR):
      International Collaboration Between Nuclear Reaction Data Centres (NRDC)
    authors:
      - family-names: Otuka
        given-names: Naohiko
      - family-names: Dupont
        given-names: Emmeric
      - family-names: Semkova
        given-names: Viktoriya
    journal: Nuclear Data Sheets
    volume: 120
    start: 272
    end: 276
    year: 2014
    doi: 10.1016/j.nds.2014.07.065
    notes: >-
      The archive this package retrieves from. Data obtained through it should cite the original
      measurements, whose EXFOR accession numbers the run record preserves.
